From abb61ad3756dcd6a900d08669cc0aaff5edf230a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jakompiled <itsrufer@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 16:52:57 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 07/11] goalc wasm: what the GOAL kernel needs

- pp and the GOAL stack pointer are mutable i64 globals shared by every
  module (env.pp, env.sp); registers pinned to r13 (pp) use env.pp and
  the symbol table register (r14) reads s7
- stack variables: 16-byte aligned frame on the GOAL stack
- (break) traps; INSTRUCTION_SET is 'wasm when compiling with goalc-wasm
- goalc-wasm: compile several files in order (--out-dir), --report and
  --trap-unsupported (unsupported functions become traps), keep names
---
