  *
  *   goalc-wasm [--game jak2] [--proj-path dir] [--no-opt] [--shared-memory] [--print-ir]
  *              <in.gc> <out.wasm | out.o>
+ *   goalc-wasm [options] [--report] --out-dir <dir> <in1.gc> <in2.gc> ...
+ *
+ * With --out-dir, the files are compiled in order by the same compiler (like a DGO build, where
+ * each file sees the types and symbols defined by the previous ones) to <dir>/<name>.o.
+ * --report lists every function the backend can't compile yet instead of stopping at the first.
+ * --trap-unsupported compiles those functions to a stub that traps, so the object still builds.
  *
  * With a .o output it writes a GOAL object file for the wasm runtime (static data, function
  * objects and the embedded module, see codegen_wasm_object) and the module next to it (.wasm).
